backstory = "Former office IT technician who kept the same fleet of PCs alive through three company rebrands. She named the printer Keith after a manager who also refused to work on Mondays. She now runs a repair table at the scrapyard and wants to prove dependable old machines deserve another job. Her niece June makes union membership cards for the refurbished desktops. Sally once took a day off and returned to find Keith promoted to Network Infrastructure. Her bluntness hides pride in teaching people to fix things themselves."
